We need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta true. There is action stage_schedule_candidate: parameters ?candidate ?loading_container ?transport_leg ?route_task_profile. Precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate. Effect: candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate.

Thus we need to stage the candidate after we have loading container loaded and leg linked, and task profile linked, and origin_leg_loaded false (we haven't loaded origin leg). We have not yet loaded origin leg onto transport leg (origin_leg_loaded). That's fine.

Thus after loading container onto leg, we can stage.

But stage_schedule_candidate also requires loading_container_loaded (true after load_container_onto_leg) and loading_container_leg_linked (true after same), candidate_task_profile_linked (we will have after attach), not origin_leg_loaded (true), not candidate_staged_for_loading (false). So we can stage.

After staging, we can verify loading profile.

Which verify action to use? Either nominal or destination flag. The difference is nominal requires not destination_leg_loaded; destination flag requires destination_leg_loaded. We have not loaded destination leg yet (destination_leg_loaded false). So we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal.

Preconditions: candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate, candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate, candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_loading_verified ?candidate.

