Thus we need to assign operator after candidate_prepared.

Skill certificate: assign_skill_certificate ?candidate ?skill_certificate. Precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate, skill_certificate_available ?skill_certificate. Effect: candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate, not skill_certificate_available ?skill_certificate.

Thus we need to assign skill certificate.

Now we also need candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha. Currently compliance_certificate_alpha is linked to shift_candidate_alpha. Need to release it from alpha then assign to beta.

We have action release_compliance_certificate ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. Precondition: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. Effect: compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_certificate, not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate.

Thus we can release from shift_candidate_alpha.

Then assign_compliance_certificate ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. Precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate, compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_certificate. Effect: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate, not compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_candidate.

Thus we need shift_candidate_beta prepared before assigning compliance.

Now candidate_finalized shift_candidate_beta: There are several finalize actions: finalize_candidate_direct, finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation, finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation.

Goal also requires dispatch_ready shift_candidate_beta and dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_beta and dispatched shift_candidate_beta.

We can achieve finalize via finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete ?candidate, not candidate_finalized). Or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized). Or finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized). Since we will have clearance established and maybe route sequence validated, we could use after sequence validation.

But we also need dispatch_ready and dispatch_allocated and dispatched. Those can be achieved via execute_schedule_dispatch action after we have dispatch_allocated, vehicle linked, dispatch slot linked, not dispatched.

Thus we need to allocate dispatch slot to shift_candidate_beta, origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha.

Goal requires candidate_dispatch_slot_linked for each of those three entities to dispatch_slot_alpha. Also dispatch_allocated true for each, dispatch_ready true, dispatched true.

We currently have dispatch_slot_alpha available. We need to allocate it to each candidate. The action allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate parameters ?candidate - candidate_entity ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile. Precondition: dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate. Effect: dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.

Thus we need each candidate to be dispatch_ready and have task profile linked before allocating dispatch slot.

We can make each candidate dispatch_ready via mark_*_availability_dispatch_ready actions: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready, mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready. For shift_candidate_beta we have no specific dispatch ready action; but we have finalize actions that set dispatch_ready as effect (finalize_candidate_direct and finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation and finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation all set dispatch_ready ?candidate). So after finalizing shift_candidate_beta, we get dispatch_ready true.

Thus we can finalize shift_candidate_beta first, then allocate dispatch slot.

But allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate (true after finalize), candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile (we will have after attach), dispatch_slot_available (still available until we allocate to first candidate), not dispatch_allocated ?candidate.

After allocating to first candidate, dispatch_slot_available becomes false, so we cannot allocate to second candidate unless we release it. However after execute_schedule_dispatch, the effect includes dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot (makes it available again). So we can allocate, then execute dispatch (which will set dispatched true, vehicle_available, dispatch_slot_available). After dispatch, slot becomes available again for next candidate.

Thus we can loop: allocate slot to candidate, execute dispatch, then slot free for next.

We need to do this for origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha, shift_candidate_beta.

Order: maybe origin first, then destination, then shift_candidate_beta.

We need each candidate to have vehicle_allocated and candidate_vehicle_linked to a vehicle unit. For origin and destination availabilities, they already have vehicle allocated (origin to vehicle_unit_alpha, destination to vehicle_unit_beta) and vehicle_allocated true. Good.

